  "statement": "# Bannerfall: Tiny Kingdoms — task brief\n\nThis is a design target, not an implementation specification. Build your own GDD, scene structure, rules, and code.\n\n## Target player experience\n\nCommand a small kingdom from the keyboard, gather and spend limited resources, grow an army, and defeat a clearly readable opposing force.\n\n## Scope boundary\n\nA small strategy game whose controls, economy, conflict, victory, failure, and restart can all be exercised through the benchmark input interface.\n\n## Required controls\n\nThis task requires at least 4 declared extended actions in `gb_levels.json.extended_actions` (extra InputMap verbs beyond the eight canonical `gb_*` actions, each bound to a real key and read in gameplay code) covering: group or unit selection; training a unit; opening build or placement; issuing an order such as attack, gather, or rally. Choose your own stable ids. Holding every declared extra from frame 0 must not clear the game.\n\n## Creative freedom\n\nYou may choose the map topology, unit statistics, pacing, and visual composition while keeping the strategic loop compact.\n"
}
